  "Question": "What is \\(2000(2000^{2000})?\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(2000^{2001}\\)",
    "B": "\\(4000^{2000}\\)",
    "C": "\\(2000^{4000}\\)",
    "D": "\\(4{,}000{,}000^{2000}\\)",
    "E": "\\(2000^{4{,}000{,}000}\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Solution": "The factor \\(2000^{2000}\\) is a product of \\(2000\\) copies of \\(2000\\). Multiplying by one more copy gives \\(2001\\) copies. Equivalently, the same-base exponent rule gives\n\\[\n2000(2000^{2000})\n=2000^1\\cdot2000^{2000}\n=2000^{2001}.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(\\boxed{2000^{2001}}\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{A}\\).",
